{"id": "EUVD-2026-97444", "enisaUuid": "450cdc7b-86eb-3f7c-ac9f-9af04d8800cf", "description": "LogicalDOC Community Edition through 9.3 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in SoapDocumentService operations that allows authenticated users to access and modify unauthorized documents. Attackers can call copy, getExtractedText, deleteVersion, reindex, deleteLink, or restore via SOAP or /services/rest/document with sequential document IDs to disclose, delete, or tamper with documents.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:39:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:16:41", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/discussions/119", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/commit/648047ee0ec95c294bb983e511fed60dbc67977f", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/blob/9.3/logicaldoc-webservice/src/main/java/com/logicaldoc/webservice/soap/endpoint/SoapDocumentService.java#L445", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/logicaldoc-community-edition-through-9.3-missing-authorization-in-documentservice"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109201", "GHSA-g833-jpqm-6g28"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03509024-b4ba-3b9a-a489-eb7652944179", "product": {"name": "LogicalDOC Community Edition", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ce084cf-01d1-3b85-acfd-eae24344e42b", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}], "isExploited": false}